This project is a modified fork of MiniOneRec
(https://github.com/AkaliKong/MiniOneRec, Apache-2.0,
technical report: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.24431)
and reuses parts of TRL (Apache-2.0).

Modified files include (not exhaustive): data.py, sft.py, rl.py,
minionerec_trainer.py, evaluate.py, calc.py, LogitProcessor.py,
ds_zero2_patches.py, convert_dataset.py, rq/rqkmeans_constrained.py,
and the training/evaluation shell scripts (sft.sh, sft_ntp.sh, rl.sh,
rl_ds.sh, evaluate.sh, eval_rl_ds_ckpts.sh, convert_dataset.sh).

Main modifications:
- Per-task dual-trie constrained decoding (full-SID trie vs 3-level
  prefix trie routed by prompt type);
- First-diff token-level rewards for GRPO (ranking_firstdiff) with
  group/column-normalized token advantages;
- DeepSpeed ZeRO-2 integration with checkpoint-engine adaptations
  (engine-state skip, best-model direct HF loading, multi-rank-safe
  run directories);
- Evaluation harness fixes (deterministic beam search, protocol
  alignment) and offline bucket/migration analysis tooling.

Change log and experiment records: docs/PROGRESS.md, docs/RL_IDEAS.md.
Method overview: README.md.
